\begin{center}

\Stone{ {$t_{n1}$}}\Stone{ {$t_{n2}$}} $\cdots$ \Stone{ {$t_{n,n-1}$}}\Stone{ {$t_{nn}$}}
[0.2pt]
\Stone{ {$t_{n-1,1}$}} $\cdots$ \Stone{ {$t_{n-1,n-1}$}}
[0.3cm]
$\cdots$ $\cdots$ $\cdots$
[0.3cm]
\Stone{ {$t_{21}$}}\Stone{ {$t_{22}$}}
[0.2pt]
\Stone{ {$t_{11}$}}

\end{center}
is called a Gelfand-Tsetlin tableau.
